    "wf-1": {
      "id": "wf-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Agents read and edit Prompt Kit documents through the Prompt Kit tools. The tools keep typed structure, stable IDs, revision checks, canonical JSON, production renders, and recovery history. Codex and Claude Code reach the tools through MCP, and pi reaches them through the installed bridge extension. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_guidance",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " serves this page as topic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workflow",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-2": {
      "id": "wf-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "When to Use the Prompt Kit Tools"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-3": {
      "id": "wf-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An agent uses the Prompt Kit tools for each read and each edit of a prompt."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-4": {
      "id": "wf-4",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Use them when a project has a Prompt Kit catalog."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-5": {
      "id": "wf-5",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Use them when the user asks you to inspect, author, or revise model-facing prompts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-6": {
      "id": "wf-6",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Never rewrite prompt JSON or rendered Markdown directly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-7": {
      "id": "wf-7",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Read-only work needs no task. A task pins the guidance and the scope, and it does not reserve a prompt."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-8": {
      "id": "wf-8",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "If the connection or a tool you need is missing, report that setup gap. Do not bypass the prompt tools."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-9": {
      "id": "wf-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Start a Task"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-10": {
      "id": "wf-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A task is the in-memory record that pins the profile and the guidance snapshot for your edits. Each write needs the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of a live task. A task expires 12 hours after "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_begin",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or after 30 minutes without a call that passes its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Expiry keeps your saved edits."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-11": {
      "id": "wf-11",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Call "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_discover",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for the active workspace, and use a project ID that it returns."
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "wf-12",
        "wf-13",
        "wf-14"
      ]
    },
    "wf-12": {
      "id": "wf-12",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Select the requested project explicitly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-13": {
      "id": "wf-13",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Pass "
        },
        {
          "insert": "project",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to list only the prompts and discovery errors of that project."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-14": {
      "id": "wf-14",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "prompts_capabilities",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lists the project IDs, the guidance topics, and the writes that each topic unlocks."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-15": {
      "id": "wf-15",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Call "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_begin",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "single-output",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "generic",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " profile that fits the prompt, and keep its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "wf-16"
      ]
    },
    "wf-16": {
      "id": "wf-16",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Without a profile, the task uses the default profile of the project."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-17": {
      "id": "wf-17",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Read "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_guidance",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with that "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and topic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "standards",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "wf-18"
      ]
    },
    "wf-18": {
      "id": "wf-18",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The service refuses "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_apply_ops",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " until the task reads every part of topic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "standards",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". One read of each part in each task is enough."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-19": {
      "id": "wf-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Edit and Check a Prompt"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-20": {
      "id": "wf-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Each edit is a typed operation batch at the current revision hash. A valid batch saves at once."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-21": {
      "id": "wf-21",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Call "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_read",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for the target. Review the production render, and pass its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "hash",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "expected_hash",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-22": {
      "id": "wf-22",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Apply typed operations with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_apply_ops",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "wf-23"
      ]
    },
    "wf-23": {
      "id": "wf-23",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "On a revision conflict, read the current document and reconcile the requested change before you retry."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-24": {
      "id": "wf-24",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Call "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_check",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and repair each required finding."
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "wf-25"
      ]
    },
    "wf-25": {
      "id": "wf-25",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "With "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", the check also reports each prompt the task changed and whether its current revision passed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-26": {
      "id": "wf-26",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Report the changed prompts and each finding you could not repair."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-27": {
      "id": "wf-27",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Read the Findings"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-28": {
      "id": "wf-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Treat structural and undeclared-variable errors as blockers. Treat prose findings as review criteria. A passing check does not replace an evaluation run."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-29": {
      "id": "wf-29",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Read the Guidance Topics"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-30": {
      "id": "wf-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Read "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_guidance",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and a topic for the detailed guidance of the task's pinned snapshot. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_capabilities",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lists all six topics. A topic over 24,576 bytes comes in parts, and each part names the next one."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-31": {
      "id": "wf-31",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Topic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "standards",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " holds the prompt authoring standards for the task's profile."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-32": {
      "id": "wf-32",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Topic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "operations",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " holds the PromptDocument model and the operation batch."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-33": {
      "id": "wf-33",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Topic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "catalog",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lists every guidance source with the topic that serves it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-34": {
      "id": "wf-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Choose a Profile"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-35": {
      "id": "wf-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The profile decides which structure rules apply. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " profile applies the agent section order. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "single-output",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " profile applies the bounded response contract. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "generic",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " profile forces neither template, and all profiles keep the structural and variable checks."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-36": {
      "id": "wf-36",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Undo a Saved Change"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-37": {
      "id": "wf-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Keep the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "changeId",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that the save returns. Call "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_undo",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with that ID as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "change_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "task_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and the saved current hash. Undo refuses an intervening edit. Read the prompt again and decide how to reconcile, instead of replacing the expected hash."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-38": {
      "id": "wf-38",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Run "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompts_check",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " on the undo revision before you report."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-39": {
      "id": "wf-39",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Recover an Interrupted Save"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-40": {
      "id": "wf-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Preserve the .prompt-kit/changes directory beside each prompt. If a save reports that canonical JSON committed before a later failure, read the current revision and let the next supported mutation recover the derived render under the store lock. Do not patch the journal or derived Markdown as a substitute."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-41": {
      "id": "wf-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A changed render layout or unrelated canonical revision requires inspecting the reported storage error. Restore the intended path and layout before you retry. Root-scoped undo does not transfer when the project root moves. The complete contract is Persistence and Recovery."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-42": {
      "id": "wf-42",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Review Scope"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "wf-43": {
      "id": "wf-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Deterministic checks do not replace judgment about clarity, contradictions, repetition, and output usefulness. No MCP tool runs a model evaluation. Request staged internal review through the prompt-editor workflow when that is the intended editing channel."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
